   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Day-Ahead Forecasting \u2014 price at t+1 \u2026 t+96, in one shot\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicts the Austrian imbalance price for **every 15-minute interval out to 24 hours**\n",
    "from a single forward pass, with the MRINN market rules imported unchanged.\n",
    "\n",
    "Horizon `h=1` is the interval being settled now; `h=96` is this time tomorrow.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why this is a rebuild, not a tweak\n",
    "\n",
    "The earlier day-ahead model was **horizon-blind**. It broadcast each signal's encoder\n",
    "output across the horizon axis and nothing else varied with `h` except the day-ahead\n",
    "price and the calendar \u2014 so recent history contributed an *identical* value at `h=1`\n",
    "and `h=96`. Measured spread across horizons with known-future ablated: `1.3e-07`, i.e.\n",
    "the same number 96 times. That is why its skill curve came out flat when it should\n",
    "rise steeply.\n",
    "\n",
    "The fix is a learned **horizon embedding** \u2014 one vector per horizon, concatenated onto\n",
    "every signal's representation and mixed by a `Dense` layer **shared across all 17\n",
    "signals**. Shared, not per-signal: 104 parameters instead of 17 \u00d7 104, which is what\n",
    "keeps the model under the 8,900-parameter MLP baseline.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What this run answers\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Question |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | Does the recurrent encoder beat MRINN's Dense encoder at a 24-hour horizon? |\n",
    "| 2 | Does a **rolling 12-month training window** beat training on all history since 2022? |\n",
    "| 3 | Is the horizon embedding actually load-bearing? |\n",
    "| 4 | What are the day-ahead price and calendar worth at 24 hours? |\n",
    "| 5 | Does more width help \u2014 the \"add neurons\" question \u2014 *within* parameter parity? |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Protocol\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Test = 2025-01-01 \u2192 2026-01-01**, the last 12 months. 35,033 rows, all four\n",
    "  seasons, price std 389.7. The old 4-month window had std 82.9 \u2014 errors here will\n",
    "  look larger, because this is a harder and more honest test.\n",
    "- **Constant LR, early stopping.** v2's cosine decay made every model worse at matched\n",
    "  config and seed (MR-GRU +0.460 AQL), because the LR annealed to zero while runs were\n",
    "  still improving.\n",
    "- **Baseline = seasonal naive** (price at the same interval yesterday). Persistence is\n",
    "  meaningless 24 hours out.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Running it\n",
    "\n",
    "Kaggle, **CPU**, Internet **off**. Attach the dataset containing `imbalance_data.csv`.\n",
    "Run with `SMOKE_TEST = True` first (~4 min), then set it `False` and *Save & Run All*."
   ]
  },
