    "## 5. The model \u2014 and the one thing that fixes it\n",
    "\n",
    "Three encoders share every other component:\n",
    "\n",
    "| | encoder over the 17 signals |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **MRINN** | `Dense` stack over a flat `(T,)` vector \u2014 no time axis |\n",
    "| **MR-LSTM** | `LSTM(H)` over a real `(T, 1)` sequence |\n",
    "| **MR-GRU** | `GRU(H)` over a real `(T, 1)` sequence |\n",
    "\n",
    "Then comes the fix. Each signal's summary is repeated across the 96 horizons, a\n",
    "**learned horizon embedding** is concatenated on, and a **shared** `Dense` mixes them.\n",
    "Without this the rule head receives identical input at `h=1` and `h=96` and the model\n",
    "is structurally incapable of being sharper at short horizons \u2014 the defect this\n",
    "notebook exists to correct.\n",
    "\n",
    "The horizon axis is then **folded into the batch axis**, so MRINN's rule functions \u2014\n",
    "written for `(N, H)` \u2014 apply unchanged at `(N\u00b796, H)` with weights shared across\n",
    "horizons. That is what \"the same rulebook applies at every horizon\" should mean.\n",
    "\n",
    "`P_DA_nemo` is substituted by the *known* day-ahead price at the target interval,\n",
    "because that is genuinely published a day ahead. And since `w_DA` averages **0.003**\n",
    "in this market \u2014 `P_EX` all but ignores the day-ahead price \u2014 the known-future block\n",
    "also gets a direct path into the representation, or the strongest available signal\n",
    "would be discarded by the rule itself."
   ]
