    "## 8. The experiment queue\n",
    "\n",
    "Priority-ordered: one seed of **every** question first, so a session that runs out of\n",
    "time still answers all of them, then extra seeds for the headline comparisons.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Run | Answers |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `gru_static` | headline \u2014 MR-GRU on all history since 2022 |\n",
    "| `mrinn_static` | the encoder control, and therefore the thesis claim |\n",
    "| `gru_rolling` | **does a rolling 12-month training window beat static?** |\n",
    "| `gru_no_hembed` | is the horizon embedding load-bearing? |\n",
    "| `gru_no_known` | what are the day-ahead price and calendar worth at 24 h? |\n",
    "| `lstm_static` | does the cell type matter at this horizon? |\n",
    "| `gru_H10` | the \"add more neurons\" question, *within* parameter parity |\n",
    "| `gru_1step` | reference: how much does h=1 give up to the one-step model? |\n",
    "\n",
    "**On the neuron advice.** It has already been tested at one step and **refuted** \u2014\n",
    "H=11 cost +0.316 AQL against H=8 across three seeds, losing on two of three. `gru_H10`\n",
    "retests it here because 96 outputs plus a horizon embedding genuinely need more\n",
    "capacity than one output did. H=12 is deliberately excluded: at 10,282 parameters it\n",
    "would break the sub-8,900 claim that is one of this project's strongest results.\n",
    "\n",
    "Set `SMOKE_TEST = True` for a ~4-minute end-to-end rehearsal before committing hours."
   ]
